{"name":"Marsh Marigold","hex":"#ffef17","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"marsh marigold","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Caltha palustris, a perennial plant with bright yellow flowers."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/marsh_marigold"}],"entries":[{"title":"Caltha palustris","blocks":[{"text":"Caltha palustris, known as marsh-marigold and kingcup, is a small to medium sized perennial herbaceous plant of the buttercup family, native to marshes, fens, ditches and wet woodland in temperate regions of the Northern Hemisphere. It flowers between April and August, dependent on altitude and latitude, but occasional flowers may occur at other times."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Caltha_palustris_plant.JPG/330px-Caltha_palustris_plant.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caltha_palustris","wikidata":"Q147192"},{"title":"Marsh","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, a marsh is a wetland that is dominated by herbaceous plants rather than by woody plants. More in general, the word can be used for any low-lying and seasonally waterlogged terrain. In Europe and in agricultural literature, low-lying meadows that require draining and embanked polderlands are also referred to as marshes or marshland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg/330px-Meadowlands_Lyndhurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marsh","wikidata":"Q30198"},{"title":"Marigold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Marigold is a yellow-orange color. It is named after the flower of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/French_marigold.jpg/330px-French_marigold.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marigold_(color)","wikidata